1.1.text:
Article 3

1. The objective of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence is to provide protection and services to victims of gender-based violence and the best interests of women and children that occur at home and/or in public places.
2. Violence as referred to in paragraph (1) may take the form of:
a. physical violence;
b. psychological violence;
c. sexual violence;
d. economic neglect; and
e. restriction of movement.

Article 1 1

1. The Regional Government is responsible for implementing efforts to prevent the occurrence of violence and protect victims of violence.
2. Prevention of the occurrence of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. collecting data and information about women and children as well as related laws and regulations;
b. conducting education on anti-violence values; and
c. disseminating laws and regulations related to the implementation of prevention and protection of victims of violence.
3. Protection of victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be in the form of:
a. establishing and facilitating the operation of integrated service institutions for victims by involving relevant agencies/institutions and community elements;
b. facilitating assistance, legal aid and legal services according to the needs of victims;
c. providing housing, both safe houses and alternative housing along with handling mechanisms, services, and psychosocial support;
d. conducting continuous handling up to the rehabilitation and social reintegration stage;
e. conducting monitoring and evaluation of the implementation of protection of victims of violence; and
f. encouraging public awareness of the importance of protection for victims of violence. 4.  In order to carry out the responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall establish programs and action activities for the protection of women and children in a Regional Action Plan for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence.

5. The Regional Action Plan for the Protection of Women and Children Victims of Violence as referred to in paragraph (2lr, shall be established for a period of 3 (three) years and stipulated by Regent's Decree.

CHAPTER II

PRINCIPLES AND OBJECTIVES

Article 2

The implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence is carried out based on the principles of:
a. respect for human rights;
b. gender equality and justice;
c. protection of victims' rights;
d. non-discrimination; and
e. best interests of the victim.

Article 8

1. Forms of services to victims of violence organized by PPT include:
a. medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical condition carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;
c. legal aid services to assist victims of violence in undergoing judicial processes;
d. first psychosocial assistance to victims conducted to identify the occurrence of violence and trauma experienced by victims;
e. assistance to victims of violence carried out by competent persons or institutions who have the expertise to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the empowerment and recovery of victims of violence and have cooperated with PPT; and
f. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and provision of economic access so that victims can be independent.
2. Service mechanisms as referred to in paragraph (1) are organized according to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) regulated by Regent Regulation.

CHAPTER III

RIGHTS OF VICTIMS

Article 4

every victim of violence has the right to obtain:
a. protection and assistance;
b. legal aid;
c. health services according to medical needs;
d. psychosocial services;
e. information; and
f. integrated services.

