Article 8

1. Forms of services to victims of violence organized by PPT include:
a. medical services in the form of treatment and recovery of physical condition carried out by medical personnel and paramedics;
b. medicolegal services constitute a form of medical service for evidentiary purposes in the legal field;
c. legal aid services to assist victims of violence in undergoing judicial processes;
d. first psychosocial assistance to victims conducted to identify the occurrence of violence and trauma experienced by victims;
e. assistance to victims of violence carried out by competent persons or institutions who have the expertise to conduct counseling, therapy and advocacy for the empowerment and recovery of victims of violence and have cooperated with PPT; and
f. economic independence services in the form of services for skills training and provision of economic access so that victims can be independent.
2. Service mechanisms as referred to in paragraph (1) are organized according to Standard Operating Procedures (SOP) regulated by Regent Regulation.

